# Local dev servers (agent-managed)

When work requires a running API, web UI, or verification after changes, **the agent should start and stop servers** instead of only telling the user to run commands.

## Defaults

| App     | Directory | Command           | Port (default) |
|---------|-----------|-------------------|----------------|
| Backend | `backend` | `npm run dev`     | `3001`         |
| Web     | `web`     | `npm run dev`     | `5173`         |

Use **`npm run dev`** for the backend during development (nodemon). Use **`npm start`** only if mimicking production or the user asks.

## Always-on LaunchAgents (preferred)

On this machine, keep both servers up via LaunchAgents (login + KeepAlive):

| Service | Label | Entrypoint |
|---------|-------|------------|
| API | `com.vettr.api` | `scripts/start-vettr-api.sh` → port `3001` |
| Web | `com.vettr.web` | `scripts/start-vettr-web.sh` → port `5173` |

### Scrape staging (Vettr-scrape worktree)

Always-on LaunchAgents for the Source Recipe Platform test lane (`/Users/jamie/Vettr-scrape`, DB `dealcheck_staging`):

| Service | Label | Port |
|---------|-------|------|
| Sidecar | `com.vettr.scrape-sidecar` | `3012` |
| API | `com.vettr.scrape-api` | `3013` |
| Worker | `com.vettr.scrape-worker` | (polls DB) |
| Web | `com.vettr.scrape-web` | `5175` |

Install / refresh: `bash /Users/jamie/Vettr-scrape/scripts/install-vettr-scrape-launchagents.sh`  
Health: `bash /Users/jamie/Vettr-scrape/scripts/vettr-scrape-healthcheck.sh`  
Admin UI: `http://localhost:5175/admin/sources`

Before starting ad-hoc `npm run dev`:

1. Check `lsof -i :3001` / `lsof -i :5173` (or `curl` health / root). For scrape staging also check `:3012` / `:3013` / `:5175`.
2. Do **not** start a duplicate listener on the same port.
3. If a LaunchAgent owns the port, **do not** `kill` it for routine restarts — use:
   - `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.vettr.api`
   - `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.vettr.web`
   - `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.vettr.scrape-api` (and scrape-web / scrape-sidecar / scrape-worker)
4. Only fall back to background `npm run dev` when LaunchAgents are unloaded / unavailable.

Logs: `~/Library/Logs/vettr/api.log`, `web.log` (and `.err`). Scrape staging: `scrape-api.log`, `scrape-web.log`, `scrape-sidecar.log`, `scrape-worker.log`.

## After starting

- Note the URL(s) for the user when relevant (e.g. `http://localhost:5173`, API `http://localhost:3001`).

## Stopping

- Do **not** stop LaunchAgent-managed servers unless the user asks.
- If the agent started an ad-hoc background server, stop that process when testing is done.
- If a server was started outside this session (and not via LaunchAgent), prefer telling the user which terminal to stop rather than killing unknown PIDs.

## Scope

- Local UI/API on this machine. Production web is Cloudflare Pages; production API is this same Mac via Cloudflare tunnel + Worker proxy (not Koyeb).
